@startuml direct-rialto-gate-mode-state
title Handshake GateMode (one per media source)
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> NONE : new source object

NONE : needData is staged
NONE : injector waits for needData, then adds segments
NONE : EOS answered once no injector is active

BLOCKED : needData is rejected (NO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES)
BLOCKED : injector WaitForGate() blocks, sample is held
BLOCKED : EOS resolution deferred until ungate

DROPPED : needData is rejected (NO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES)
DROPPED : new samples discarded at once, never blocks
DROPPED : generation was bumped, waiters abort

NONE --> BLOCKED : SetGate(true)\nConfigure(), CreateMediaSource(),\nFlush() flushable path
NONE --> DROPPED : Unblock()\nFlush(), Stop(), Configure(recreate),\nNotifyInjectorToPause(), UnblockTrackInjection(),\n~AampRialtoPlayer()
BLOCKED --> DROPPED : Unblock()\n(same callers; generation++)
DROPPED --> BLOCKED : SetGate(true)\nFlush() after its Unblock(),\nConfigure(position-pending)
BLOCKED --> NONE : SetGate(false)\nUngateAllSources()
DROPPED --> NONE : SetGate(false)\nUngateAllSources()

note bottom
  Ungate (SetGate(false)) only where playback really resumes:
  IssuePlay(), StartPreRoll(), Pause(false), StopBuffering(),
  NotifyInjectorToResume(), and Flush() on a non-flushable state.
  The PLAYING notification does NOT ungate.
  Reset() (new session) leaves the gate mode unchanged on purpose.
end note
@enduml
